  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribution to the Aswan International Women&apos;s Film Festival.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A few Dutch artists from the filmmaking industry are taking part in this year&apos;s edition of the Aswan International Film Festival. There will be a Dutch movie in the official short movie competition, a Dutch director among the festival&apos;s jury and a Dutch filmmaker providing workshops on the sidelines of the festival. An animation movie about migration (funded by the Dutch embassy) will also be screened and discussed at a panel discussion during the festival. This is why there is a need to support the Dutch filmmakers and increase their visibility in Egypt as well as promote knowledge and cultural exchange between both countries on the filmmaking level. This will also probably open the door for further cooperation of Dutch filmmakers with other film festivals in Egypt and thereby serve the goals of the International Dutch Cultural Policy which aims at strengthening Dutch cultural presence around the world and exchange of cultural knowledge.</narrative>
  </description>
